{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time","id":1000050,"title":"How vampires pass the time.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T17:48:58-08:00","id":1000050,"title":"How vampires pass the time.","content":"So while sitting here waiting for the next installment of content it got me thinking, how do vampires pass the time. <br /> <br /> I know some elders plot schemes and set things into motions that take decades to come to fruition. But what about the other 300ish days of the year?<br /> <br /> Sure they could socialize. <br /> They can protect their domain and holdings. <br /> <br /> What else. <br /> <br /> If we had to say, what are some of the most popular kindred hobbies to pass the time?<br /> <br /> Sports seems like an obvious thing. For millenia there have been challenges of athletic prowess. <br /> <br /> Games<br /> <br /> Movies<br /> <br /> Etc. <br /> <br /> How many elders would pick up an Xbox controller just for the hell of it?<br /> <br /> What would be your pass time if you were a kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:41:58-08:00","id":1000139,"title":"","content":"The clan books get into some of this, but I've always seen it as the reason for the Requiem to begin with. Without something to do, one wastes away or goes mad. Idle hands and all. The covenants give you some focus when you're not part of the rat race anymore.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't give up all my hobbies, but finding sources of blood would be a necessity. Something to constantly work on, even if it's only sparingly like tending a garden. There's not a lot of places open late and I'd probably resort to illegal activities to keep things going. Exploring blood sorcery would be a neat addition to hobbies, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:18:17-08:00","id":1000149,"title":"","content":"Yeah, vampires spend time on their Requiem and their Unlife, because otherwise they'd devolve into draugr more often. If memory serves, the 2e book mentions an Elder learning how to use twitter, so I could definitely see some bored Elder picking up the latest game system that all of the Neonates are talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:12:08-08:00","id":1000211,"title":"","content":"My Daeva owns a comic book store. When she's not doing scut work for her sire, she's usually hanging out there because a) her customers are her herd, and b) she genuinely likes video games and comic books. Of course, she's only been a Kindred for a little over a year, so she's still very much in touch with her humanity. She considers her regulars (herd) her friends still, and the eventual frenzy and accidental killing of one of them will really hit her hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:14:59-08:00","id":1000228,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking about comic stores, as that's one of my hobbies. I've never seen one that was open past seven, even when I lived in cities with more active night lives.<br /> <br /> Not that there couldn't be, mind, I think in general it's one of those things that makes a larger dent in the 'life' of vampires than people might think.<br /> <br /> I'd think most vampires would use the Internet for one reason or another. Not even just gaming but there's all sorts of information out there. I was thinking genealogy would be a big draw for vampires Embraced within the past few hundred years. It would be interesting to realize familial connections one couldn't make while alive, for whatever reason. Dangerous, too, considering what enemies can do about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2016, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T08:40:32-08:00","id":1000284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000228#post1000228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking about comic stores, as that's one of my hobbies. I've never seen one that was open past seven, even when I lived in cities with more active night lives.<br /> <br /> Not that there couldn't be, mind, I think in general it's one of those things that makes a larger dent in the 'life' of vampires than people might think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The store I used to hang at (it's closed now) used to close around 7ish too, but there was very often events that were later, game tournaments and the like. Also, the core of us that hung around a lot were friends enough with the owner that we hang around after closing most nights, we would chat with the owner while he counted the money and such. Also helped clean up and put books away. Sounds like the environment <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1257_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1257\" data-vbnamecard=\"1257\">Kerensky</a> 's character has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:24:59-08:00","id":1000353,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the unlife of vampires would parallel our own to a significant degree. That is, much of our lives are spent feeding ourselves and ensuring our &quot;space&quot; is in working order; the rest of it is consumed with family and social engagements that help to keep us connected and safe. A small amount of time (&lt; 10%) goes toward entertainment and self-advancement. All this has only recently changed through highly-efficient logistics and time-saving appliances.<br /> <br /> So your average night is going to be spent on:<br /> 1. Waking and ensuring you are not in a critical situation. This could involve a quick security check and/or meeting with those who maintain such things. Analogous to checking your email, if you will, and even during nights before electricity you'd have reports to absorb (verbal and written) and key, immediate decisions to make. Less-critical management decisions may wait, but can't be pushed back too far; this includes things related to your passive income streams, if any.<br /> <br /> 2. Getting your nightly food. This could be very time-consuming if you have to hunt--on the order of 4-6 hours depending on the distance to hunting grounds, quality of prey and quantity of danger you're willing to put up with. A live-in herd cuts this time dramatically and is the main reason to invest in it as well as the financial resources to keep said herd in order--but that investment is going to demand more management and social time!<br /> <br /> 3. Dealing with the social BS of your herd, help, family (ghouls and otherwise) and/or enemies/interlopers. If you do not attend to this point you will shortly not have a herd, help or family, but will have plenty of interlopers. Keep in mind that the more ghouls (trustworthy help, given how vulnerable you are and how illegal your activities) the more hunting is required.<br /> <br /> And while you can compress the time taken for any of 1, 2 or 3, the <i><b>overall</b></i> amount of time is going to be similar and eat up the majority of your average night. Many nights it will eat up ALL of your time (especially during summer) and you'll collapse into your coffin going &quot;wtf did my evening go?&quot; Please remember, you have to spend <i><b>extra</b></i> blood to just stay awake past sunrise in a misreable state of mind. I'm mortal--as are most of you, and we get to stay awake after sundown for free!<br /> <br /> If you have extra time left, or push off feeding and social for a time (a night, or several), then you can carve out attention for:<br /> <br /> 4. Improving or maintaining your professional tools: outfits, equipment, weapons and research (tools of the mind) take constant care or they lose value. Just because you (the vampire) stay the same does not mean your haven can get by without a thousand little fixes to keep it functioning, that your equipment is not being eaten by moths and worms or rusted by water while you sleep. This could include locating and preparing additional havens, following up information sources and leads, developing herd and income streams, and etc. <i><b>This is all work.</b></i> If you ignore it you'll pretty soon find things you rely on failing. Rebuilding is a huge undertaking and one of the cruelties of torpor.<br /> <br /> 5. Hobbies. Following up genealogies for fun or breeding experiments. Practicing sports or swordplay in the age of explosives. Defeating the Primogen council in a fierce contest of networked Mario Kart. Scrapbooking and journaling. Trolling RPG forums. And etc. If your vampire has much time for these items then they are skilled, well-invested, wealthy and probably capable of thinking of extremely useful measures to prepare for the next night, or night after next, when they have to deal with X or Y or Z that might rip apart their world and/or literally consume them in fire or fangs.<br /> <br /> Which is why most of the time vampires who have satisfied 1, 2, and 3 are at social engagements of a private, city or Covenant nature, making sure their fair-weather friends and all-weather enemies are not misbehaving, and figuring out the next chess moves to ensure they stay safe and well-fed.<br /> <br /> All of the above is why I can look at a vampiric elder's write-up (especially in VtM), see &quot;modest&quot; stats and think &quot;yeah, he's been busy&quot;. Because you don't get much XP for just keeping things static, even if you're wrangling deals and intimidating stiffs it's not new and not a learning experience. It's just necessary.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 11-08-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:44:18-08:00","id":1000515,"title":"","content":"Nofather:<br /> Yeah I considered that. It seems likely the only way an elder prior to the digital age would even be able to visit shops on a regular basis would be to send ghoul's in their place, and even then many places still close relatively early even now. Probably another important reason kindred stay in larger cities other than food. <br /> <br /> Wow nice writeup Khanwulf. <br /> Some of that had occurred to me but many of those points are something important to consider. <br /> <br /> I was wondering how common anachronistic tendencies would be, but it seems likely many kindred would have that problem. <br /> <br /> I see lots of people who rely heavily on their land line telephone even now, despite how common cell phones have become.<br /> <br /> So perhaps the elder that would pick up on the things we take for granted would be far fewer than I first thought. <br /> <br /> The limited time kindred have of Night hadn't played to heavily into what I was thinking, thanks for pointing it out. <br /> <br /> As for my current character. She has been a kindred for 2 years and is currently in charge of the local dragon chapter house... as there are only 3 left of the 15 - 20ish there were. <br /> <br /> Her hobbies are crashing frat parties, dancing at clubs, and throwing wrenches in her own plans apparently.<br /> <br /> She chose to cross entertainment and food with the crashing frat parties and dancing at clubs I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","user":"overload","date":". 11-08-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:46:28-08:00","id":1000677,"title":"","content":"Strange. I can think of two comic book/game stores here that are open until 10pm, at least. I think the comic book store next to the IMAX is open until 11pm on some nights. There's a lot of foot traffic there.<br /> <br /> \u200bBasically, she tends shop on her nights off until it's time to close, then it's time to take care of personal business, like Khanwulf talked about. Having a herd is hard work, especially when you care about how their lives are going.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:31:13-08:00","id":1000842,"title":"","content":"Honestly I doubt most vampires have much free time. How often do you hear &quot;there aren't enough hours in the day&quot; from real life people? And we only sleep about 8 hours, and that's a very flexible 8 hours - we have the luxury of being to stay up late and even &quot;pull an all-nighter&quot; as the need arises. Vampires though, they don't have a choice. 12 out of every 24 hours, give or take a couple hours depending on the location and time of year, they're confined indoors and heavily penalized for staying active. Feeding takes up at least one of those hours every night, possibly more if they're unlucky. Having a herd can cut down on hunting time, but requires other maintenance, so it's probably a wash in terms of time. I guess they don't necessarily have to work 40 hours a week, but I imagine Covenant responsibilities are comparable to a full-time job. Then there's elders to rub elbows with, political gambits to enact, minions to manipulate, a Cacophany to keep up to date on... A vampire who has free time is a vampire who won't make it very far up the ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:45:40-08:00","id":1000846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000842#post1000842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I doubt most vampires have much free time. How often do you hear &quot;there aren't enough hours in the day&quot; from real life people? And we only sleep about 8 hours, and that's a very flexible 8 hours - we have the luxury of being to stay up late and even &quot;pull an all-nighter&quot; as the need arises. Vampires though, they don't have a choice. 12 out of every 24 hours, give or take a couple hours depending on the location and time of year, they're confined indoors and heavily penalized for staying active. Feeding takes up at least one of those hours every night, possibly more if they're unlucky. Having a herd can cut down on hunting time, but requires other maintenance, so it's probably a wash in terms of time. I guess they don't necessarily have to work 40 hours a week, but I imagine Covenant responsibilities are comparable to a full-time job. Then there's elders to rub elbows with, political gambits to enact, minions to manipulate, a Cacophany to keep up to date on... A vampire who has free time is a vampire who won't make it very far up the ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though that assumes the full scope of Kindred society. A small-town (relatively speaking) vampire doesn't have as much vampire politics to keep up on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:53:45-08:00","id":1000853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000846#post1000846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though that assumes the full scope of Kindred society. A small-town (relatively speaking) vampire doesn't have as much vampire politics to keep up on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I assumed larger-scale Kindred society, but there would certainly be more free time for vampires in smaller and/or less cutthroat Domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:48:28-08:00","id":1000882,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind plus, Overlord.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000853#post1000853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. I assumed larger-scale Kindred society, but there would certainly be more free time for vampires in smaller and/or less cutthroat Domains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even sure smaller domains would help much, unless they're highly concentrated (like an island) or the vampire enjoys a stable herd of sufficient size. Lower-scale Kindred society usually means lower-scale populations, which are more sensitive to predation and tend to be more spread-out, increasing travel times. And that's part of the problem: travel times. You'd have to lair on top of your feeding source in order to enjoy a minimum 1 hour/night consumption time. Most hunting grounds would be described as &quot;dangerous&quot; after dark and require substantial care in ensuring the vampire does not become prey themselves or otherwise have cover blown. <br /> <br /> Hunting grounds that are &quot;secure&quot; mean there has been a considerable investment in developing them (including ghouls and other mortal contacts/conditioning), which also need to be maintained.<br /> <br /> Your absolute lowest-maintenance vampire is going to be of intimidating personal power and wealth but withdrawn from societies, with a stable on-site herd of good size and highly competent help, lairing in a secure location probably by virtue of its remote-ness. If this sounds like Dracula in his mountain fastness, or Nos in the sewers, I don't think that's accidental. These are also the models most likely to risk detachment because they are not part of human society, though a mortal herd as touchstones could help.<br /> <br /> &quot;Country&quot; vampires will spend almost all their time hunting (travel time), and city vampires trade hunting/travel time for socializing time to create their safe space. In both cases you could argue the vampires lack the wherewithall in power and money to maintain distance for their own amusements. (All this is essentially a model of human, mortal behavior by the way.)<br /> <br /> Time periods before much urbanization will just look like more country and less city. Any sufficiently powerful vampire (i.e. a little Majesty or Obfuscate) will want even more to latch themselves to a decent baron or above and feed quietly from their &quot;herd&quot; of hangers-on, as they will have one of the most concentrated groups of humanity outside of army camps, ships at sea and city squalor.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:17:15-08:00","id":1000900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000882#post1000882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the kind plus, Overlord.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not even sure smaller domains would help much, unless they're highly concentrated (like an island) or the vampire enjoys a stable herd of sufficient size. Lower-scale Kindred society usually means lower-scale populations, which are more sensitive to predation and tend to be more spread-out, increasing travel times. And that's part of the problem: travel times. You'd have to lair on top of your feeding source in order to enjoy a minimum 1 hour/night consumption time. Most hunting grounds would be described as &quot;dangerous&quot; after dark and require substantial care in ensuring the vampire does not become prey themselves or otherwise have cover blown.<br /> <br /> Hunting grounds that are &quot;secure&quot; mean there has been a considerable investment in developing them (including ghouls and other mortal contacts/conditioning), which also need to be maintained.<br /> <br /> Your absolute lowest-maintenance vampire is going to be of intimidating personal power and wealth but withdrawn from societies, with a stable on-site herd of good size and highly competent help, lairing in a secure location probably by virtue of its remote-ness. If this sounds like Dracula in his mountain fastness, or Nos in the sewers, I don't think that's accidental. These are also the models most likely to risk detachment because they are not part of human society, though a mortal herd as touchstones could help.<br /> <br /> &quot;Country&quot; vampires will spend almost all their time hunting (travel time), and city vampires trade hunting/travel time for socializing time to create their safe space. In both cases you could argue the vampires lack the wherewithall in power and money to maintain distance for their own amusements. (All this is essentially a model of human, mortal behavior by the way.)<br /> <br /> Time periods before much urbanization will just look like more country and less city. Any sufficiently powerful vampire (i.e. a little Majesty or Obfuscate) will want even more to latch themselves to a decent baron or above and feed quietly from their &quot;herd&quot; of hangers-on, as they will have one of the most concentrated groups of humanity outside of army camps, ships at sea and city squalor.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, given a tank size of 10 (at minimum) and a consumption rate of at least 1 per night, a vampire might not need to feed every night. Minimum Herd size is about 2 (1 Lethal taking 2 days to heal). If there aren't other demands upon the vampire's Vitae (such as from combat, or politics), then that is fairly sustainable no matter where you are. Obviously, there is very little slack in such an arrangement, so higher Herd numbers or reliable &quot;emergency&quot; feeding locations are ideal. But it isn't impossible.<br /> <br /> A &quot;country&quot; vampire could probably manage 4-5 Herd reliably without significant travel time, and leave hunting for when Vitae demands outstrip the average consumption rate. Social obligations to said Herd will of course vary. Some are more independent than others.<br /> <hr /><br /> Obviously, if you can find mortals with Merits like Quick Healer and/or Biokinesis (which boost healing times), all the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T21:04:35-08:00","id":1001178,"title":"","content":"So I guess the big take away here is Retainer is actually one of the more important merits by the thought process of limited time.<br /> <br /> More retainers with diversity could help keep a kindred up to date on current trends, technology, etc as well as take care of more mundane tasks to save the kindred precious night time.<br /> <br /> I could see elder kindred cultivating whole city blocks over time for ease of feeding and personal safety. I suppose this would consume a great deal of time, leaving very little room for hobbies unless you work them in as part of your career.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T21:23:01-08:00","id":1001181,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ghouls are important.<br /> <br /> It's something you can still work around, however. Clan book Mekhet has a vampire who lives in a building with a group of women, she uses Obfuscate to hide and sneaks down to feed from them occasionally. I believe there's some other Influence to keep them out of the crawlspace she beds in. I had a similar vampire who 'worked' on the Metrorail, sort of acting like the Trainman from the Matrix. Very hostile to other vampires, but otherwise remained constantly Obfuscated and he would just wait to feed on travelers.<br /> <br /> I find the Mabry interesting, as they are sort of solitary but sentinel and have an interesting predatory scheme. But I'm a less a fan of organized 'bring me another kine,' feeding..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:15:49-08:00","id":1001282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1001178#post1001178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess the big take away here is Retainer is actually one of the more important merits by the thought process of limited time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Staff is even more important.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:27:54-08:00","id":1001406,"title":"","content":"Retainers, Herd, staff. Domain. It's all about domain and what's &quot;yours&quot; within it. Which circles back to the core concept of the vampire as a hidden predator and why the books focus on city politics as being centered around domain squabbles or influence plays (to gain control over domain).<br /> <br /> It's a surprisingly tight thematic bundle, really.<br /> <br /> If you have decent attributes and skills, and the right disciplines, then that really makes hunting easier. The questions that follow are only &quot;what else do you need to do to maintain your domain&quot;--and if it's as small as a single house or subway platform then the answer may be &quot;not much&quot;--even the prince may not care to have you check in often, though a wise sheriff would confirm you're still active periodically.<br /> <br /> And this can apply to travel time as well: being able to turn into a bird or bat does wonders for covering ground, and low-level presence doesn't even cost blood to activate, so it won't increase your feeding requirements as dominate would. There has to be as many solutions to the core vampiric problem of sustenance as there are vampires, but it will revolve around ensuring a safe, productive domain.<br /> <br /> Let's talk hobbies, however. If your Kindred isn't up to their earrings in local socializing and relationships (and assuming those aren't her main hobby), she'll still have SOME free time left--an hour, maybe two for something. Yoga. Stamps. Casual torture. Usual stuff. So the thought that should follow is &quot;how much does maintaining this hobby cost in resources?&quot; Resources in money (which has to be earned from some income stream). Resources in security concerns (have size is larger for your collection of welded used prosthetic art, after all) and maintenance.<br /> <br /> Further, this being an RPG with advancement as a core concept, hobbies for players and key NPCs are likely to be ones that are <i><b>active</b></i>. They take the vamp out of the attic, give the opportunity for skill practice, have an inherent risk (personal harm, security loss, resource cost) associated and therefore provide a chance of improvement in skill-levels. Which means they take even more time to indulge in (&quot;Sorry Gridley--tonight's bowling. You'll have to manage the ticker yourself and let me know how that argument with the missus' works out. Ta-ta!&quot;).<br /> <br /> Digression: Is this a good time to point out how fantastic Gilded Cage &quot;Red Light&quot; would be for totally exasperating an opponent in just their <i>normal</i> operating affairs? Give it a month: the frustration would be tangible next Elysium! <br /> <br /> So here's a question: assuming a character is operating in a fashion where they can get an hour or two of 'free' time a night to pursue personal development, how long before they accumulate an XP point?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:05:34-08:00","id":1001479,"title":"","content":"Perhaps not the most stereotypical of vampires, but one of mine runs a nightclub full of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Sort of cliche' ( but based off a book ) he named his club Circus of the Damned and they do a lot of performing. So a lot of his time is spent socializing with guests and clients, building relationships with other supernaturals ( changelings and werecats mostly. ) this is both a profession and a hobby as he also performs at the club and enjoys what he does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T17:26:27-08:00","id":1001553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1001406#post1001406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So here's a question: assuming a character is operating in a fashion where they can get an hour or two of 'free' time a night to pursue personal development, how long before they accumulate an XP point?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo more than a beat per session, I'd say, and only if there's some meaningful interaction or roleplaying associated with the activity. Passively sitting in your haven, pressing stamps into a book? Nope. Negotiating favors with a fellow philatelist to acquire the missing 1855 10 cent green Washington for your pre-Civil War collection? Yeah, you're getting a beat for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T21:06:50-08:00","id":1001617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1001553#post1001553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo more than a beat per session, I'd say, and only if there's some meaningful interaction or roleplaying associated with the activity. Passively sitting in your haven, pressing stamps into a book? Nope. Negotiating favors with a fellow philatelist to acquire the missing 1855 10 cent green Washington for your pre-Civil War collection? Yeah, you're getting a beat for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I was thinking. If it's important enough for your character to devote enough time to get a beat, at least be a little creative with the justification. That would be my only stipulation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:42:48-08:00","id":1001753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1001553#post1001553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo more than a beat per session, I'd say, and only if there's some meaningful interaction or roleplaying associated with the activity. Passively sitting in your haven, pressing stamps into a book? Nope. Negotiating favors with a fellow philatelist to acquire the missing 1855 10 cent green Washington for your pre-Civil War collection? Yeah, you're getting a beat for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I may have been unclear however. I was actually thinking along the lines of downtime between sessions, for chronicles that skip time. So given a period of nominally &quot;normal&quot; activity between more intense story segments, how much might be appropriate? A beat? Which period (month, year, etc.)?<br /> <br /> Context: This, to me, is the real appeal of vampires for storytelling: you can tell long-running tales that collide with history--either dredged from the past or set within it. This means research and writing as the medium for the stories, instead of tabletop play, as befits my now far-flung gaming partners.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:47:55-08:00","id":1002077,"title":"","content":"Oh, for downtime purposes? I would say it depends on how long the downtime is. I swear there is a section in one of the books that details guidelines for experience gain during downtime, but I can't find it. As a general rule, I usually go with one beat per year, or two experience per decade. It may sound stingy to some, but my thinking is that if it's not important enough to be covered in an actual session with roleplaying, it's not important enough to get a good reward for it. For shorter timespans, you may want to up it to a beat per six months or in extreme cases, a beat per month. I would only be that generous if the downtime was limited to one or two years, though.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat of course, is my rule for experience and downtime in general. As pertaining to a specific hobby, you might have the same distribution of beats, but I would probably only allow that experience to apply to a narrow window of skills and merits related to that specific hobby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:55:44-08:00","id":1002081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1001753#post1001753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks! I may have been unclear however. I was actually thinking along the lines of downtime between sessions, for chronicles that skip time. So given a period of nominally &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; activity between more intense story segments, how much might be appropriate? A beat? Which period (month, year, etc.)?<br /> <br /> Context: This, to me, is the real appeal of vampires for storytelling: you can tell long-running tales that collide with history--either dredged from the past or set within it. This means research and writing as the medium for the stories, instead of tabletop play, as befits my now far-flung gaming partners.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thought on downtime xp. <br /> Decide how much you want to give.<br /> Come up with a list of leading questions about how the pc spends this time. By leading I mean try to get them to name the what, when, where, why, who. <br /> <br /> The pc gets xp and you get more plot hooks.<br /> Probably wouldn't go over 1 xp per downtime, maybe less if it's under a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:46:12-08:00","id":1002989,"title":"","content":"Thanks folks, much appreciate the comments--very useful.<br /> <br /> I'll add a few thoughts: there are, broadly, two types of downtime. The first takes place between play sessions when the characters have reached a state of &quot;normal&quot; and their main distractions are the usual from life. Generally speaking during this period of time characters will be unfocused and do whatever is necessary to maintain existence at the desired level of comfort, with their free time sliced off toward a variety of interests. Beat (XP) generation is going to be slow, primarily because the characters are not pushing themselves in this environment--if they were, then you'd semi-play it out as per the next type.<br /> <br /> The second downtime type is what you might otherwise call the &quot;montage scene&quot;, in which there is a break of some length in the main story but the characters are strongly motivated to prepare in a specific direction for their goals. The Storyteller keeps the focus on the characters and their action following the basic ideas of their direction, and then resumes episodic play. Beat generation will be faster but likely limited toward advancing the key interest being practiced. You can have a montage scene that lasts years or decades (Conner in Highlander is an example of this), but the end result will tend to be &quot;the Storyteller wants me to have X at Y level&quot; in that case. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:48:28-08:00","id":1003110,"title":"","content":"For some reason I've always imagined that vampires, especially the older ones pick up writing. After all, lord knows they're unlives gives them plenty of material to work with and even if they have to alter a few things to not have a hunter's goldmine, a handbook for the local vampires and their social structures and such, lying around their haven. Also eventually they'll have to take a nap, so having a written record would probably be a huge help in parcing real memories from dream fabrication. And after all why should Dracula and Lestat get all the fun, when any vampire's life story could be just as if not more interesting/insane then theirs.<br /> <br /> The internet is also probably a blessing for vampires. All the world at their fingertips 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year. I can imagine some vampire rising from a sleep they entered back in the horse and buggy, pony express days, weeping bloody tears of joy upon discovering the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 11-14-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:58:32-08:00","id":1003143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1003110#post1003110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason I've always imagined that vampires, especially the older ones pick up writing. After all, lord knows they're unlives gives them plenty of material to work with and even if they have to alter a few things to not have a hunter's goldmine, a handbook for the local vampires and their social structures and such, lying around their haven. Also eventually they'll have to take a nap, so having a written record would probably be a huge help in parcing real memories from dream fabrication. And after all why should Dracula and Lestat get all the fun, when any vampire's life story could be just as if not more interesting/insane then theirs.<br /> <br /> The internet is also probably a blessing for vampires. All the world at their fingertips 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year. I can imagine some vampire rising from a sleep they entered back in the horse and buggy, pony express days, weeping bloody tears of joy upon discovering the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until they realize any idiot can post anything and have it declared the truth and all of a sudden everything they learned on the Internet is suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T20:14:22-08:00","id":1003213,"title":"","content":"I imagine a civic arts center would be a hilariously productive Touchstone. There's always that one quiet student in the back of every damn class...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:01:56-08:00","id":1003395,"title":"","content":"Dude they got 12 hours a night, there's barely enough time for every night activities like showering, dressing up (and doing make up), hunting, visiting Elysium (for the especially social types) and doing whatever night-shift that pays the bills. Passing time? They barely got enough time.<br /> <br /> Ps. I am mostly talking about neonates here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 11-15-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:11:53-08:00","id":1003401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000149#post1000149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, vampires spend time on their Requiem and their Unlife, because otherwise they'd devolve into draugr more often. If memory serves, the 2e book mentions an Elder learning how to use twitter, so I could definitely see some bored Elder picking up the latest game system that all of the Neonates are talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the characters I've seen in a Masquerade game was a Tremere elder who got a little too preoccupied with video games, which has lead to crazy rumors in Court. Some even thought he was hiding torpor or plotting to take over the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:20:58-08:00","id":1003405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1000050-how-vampires-pass-the-time?p=1000228#post1000228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking about comic stores, as that's one of my hobbies. I've never seen one that was open past seven, even when I lived in cities with more active night lives.<br /> <br /> Not that there couldn't be, mind, I think in general it's one of those things that makes a larger dent in the 'life' of vampires than people might think.<br /> <br /> I'd think most vampires would use the Internet for one reason or another. Not even just gaming but there's all sorts of information out there. I was thinking genealogy would be a big draw for vampires Embraced within the past few hundred years. It would be interesting to realize familial connections one couldn't make while alive, for whatever reason. Dangerous, too, considering what enemies can do about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's the World of Darkness, people are naturally more nocturnal in this world than the real one, I don't think it would be far fetched if some comic book stores stayed open beyond real life closing hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}